some people associate instant noodles  with broke college students but instant  ramen wasn't created for a bunch of  hungry 20 year olds the man who invented  them was much more ambitious he set out  to solve a hunger crisis in Japan after  World War two food shortages plagued  Japanese cities so the u.s. supplied  wheat flour and encouraged the Japanese  to make bread one man named Momofuku  Ando didn't understand why his people  would make bread instead of noodles  something that was already part of their  culture undo decided to take matters  into his own hands and create a new  ramen made to last he spent a year  trying to figure out how to preserve the  noodles he needed a non perishable tasty  and easy recipe but it was a challenge  to maintain the robust flavors and  unique texture that most people were  accustomed to it wasn't until his wife  was making dinner one night and he threw  some noodles in a bowl of hot tempura  oil that he realized flash frying the  noodles was the answer he had been  looking for this method not only  dehydrated them  it left small perforations that allowed  the noodles to recut quickly and there  you have it instant ramen noodles became  an instant success undos products gained  notoriety when he introduced the  packaged ramen in the 1950s and later  cup noodles in 1978 his company began  selling upwards of 40 billion units  every year and Momofuku ndu became a  culinary icon in Japan  so the next time you heat up a cup of  instant noodles remember you're slurping  down a little piece of history
 

